3. seed engine

    state space

        entropy source `os.urandom(32)` at generation time

        state space 2^256, about 1.15 * 10^77 possible dimensions (1.159 undecillion where the web is only about 18 quintillion). all 32 bytes drive the picture. (I shortened it to 16 for a day so the seed was pasteable, then put it back: the identity and the picture should be the same number, and that number is this one)

        hash blake3 of `"CHAOS-SEED-v2" || ticket_id(16) || client_random(32) || instance_id(16)` (the ticket is what the server gives you for one roll, see 11. no ticket = preview roll)

        stream `xoshiro256**` seeded from the 32 byte hash

        sub streams independent xoshiro instances, one per system: rarity, shape, mutation, skin, palette, lights, motion, satellites, twin, planes, debris, particles, rings, background, mood, mode, runtime. each is blake3(seed_full || label) so adding a system later does not disturb existing seeds (done, v0.2)

    shareable forms

        seed_full: 32 bytes, 64 hex. the registry identity, what the .chaos file and the website key on. collision proof, nobody types this.

        base58: the whole 32 bytes, 43 or 44 chars, bitcoin alphabet. the display in the corner and what goes in seed_display in the file. `chaos --seed <it>` replays. (done, v0.4)

        seed_short: first 8 bytes as 16 hex. a display prefix and the vault file name, like a git short hash. does not replay anything on its own

        words: bip39, 24 words (256 bits + 8 bit sha256 checksum, the standard). `chaos --seed "word word ..."` replays. checked against the trezor vectors. for humans saying it out loud (done, v0.4)

        .chaos: the 512 byte file. not a seed, a claim ticket. see 11.

        url: `chaos://<base58>` later maybe, so a link opens the app. (not planned, if adhd allows)

    rng api (done)

        `uniform()` [0,1), `range(lo,hi)`, `rangeInt(lo,hi)` inclusive like the js, `chance(p)`, `jump()` 2^128 steps

        xoshiro all-zero state is the one state it cannot leave, so a zero seed gets kicked to a constant. (yes someone will try)

4. shapes (done, v0.2)

    41 generators, ported from the web buildShape. 0..39 real, 40 compound (2 to 4 others fused, each thrown into its own orientation and scale)

    torus knot, supershape, wobble torus, icosahedron, octahedron, dodecahedron, box, sphere, cylinder, cone, ring, plane, lathe, spiral shell, saddle sheet, corkscrew, fluted torus, ribbed cylinder, rippled sphere, sinc ripple, torus arc, spline tube, lathe pod, lissajous knot, harmonic blob, klein bottle, mobius band, berry cluster, fractal flake, gyroid sheet, conch, superellipsoid, braid, enneper, dini, roman surface, voxel colony, clelia spiral, urchin, rose lathe, compound

    the three.js geometry zoo had to be rewritten (there is no three.js in c++, obviously): box, plane, cylinder/cone, ring, torus, torus knot, lathe, tube (catmull-rom centripetal + parallel transport frames), polyhedron with subdivision (icosa/octa/tetra/dodeca), parametric. plus merge, transform, weld (mergeVertices). all in client/src/shape/primitives.cpp, about 350 lines

    weld before mutate: compound and merged shapes come back with seams and the vertex shader pushes along the normal, so without the weld every face tears apart. same trick as the web

    mutation lineage: gen 0 is twist, maybe warp (60%), ripple. then 1 to 4 more gens picked from twist, warp, ripple, noise, swirl, bulge/pinch, shear, fold. each gen works on the output of the last and is a bit stronger (0.6 + 0.3 * gen). the app prints the lineage like the web console did

    family ids for the .chaos file (0..15): the 41 generators bucketed into 16 families for rarity and value. knots, superformula, tori, polyhedra, primitives, lathes, shells, sheets, ribbed, tubes, minimal, clusters, colonies, compound, 14 reserved for mythic, 15 reserved. table in client/src/seed/rarity.cpp, mirrored as a comment in shared/chaos_format.h (done, v0.4). the generator id itself is not in the file, the seed replays it

    not ported: nothing. everything in buildShape is in. the vertex counts are a bit different because the parametric grids aer mine not three's, nobody will notice

5. skin + shaders (done, v0.2)

    berry skin: ported 1:1 from BERRY_VERT / BERRY_FRAG. glsl 430 core, `in/out` instead of varying, `fragColor` instead of gl_FragColor, `uProj`/`uModelView` instead of the three.js built-ins. the common block (hash, noise, fbm, voronoi) is a `#include <berry_common.glsl>` my shader loader expands

    lights are fed in model space like the web (feedBerry: cam and 3 light dirs multiplied by the inverse model matrix per mesh)

    hyperspace backdrop: same shader, drawn on the inside of a radius 90 sphere parked on the camera, no culling, depth off. (first time it rendered black cuz I never cleared depth. don't ask)

    satellites: 2 to 14, 55% wear the berry skin with their own smaller params, the rest use the glitch shader (5 modes, same as web)

    fold planes, debris: MeshPhongMaterial does not exist here so phong.frag is a stand in: lambert / pi, blinn-phong normalised, 3 directional + ambient + emissive + linear fog 60..240. close enough, the duotone eats the hue anyway

    rings: MeshBasicMaterial, half of them wireframe (glPolygonMode line)

    particles: 400 to 900 points, additive, size attenuated, drifting and slowly rotating like the web

    wire ghost: the main shape again at 1.01 scale, white lines, alpha 0.04..0.16

    shadows: not ported. the web had a 2048 shadow map on the key light. after the duotone you can barely tell. maybe v1.3 polish, maybe never

    msaa: 4x on the scene target, resolved before post. the web had antialias:true

6. post stack (done, v0.2)

    render (hdr, rgba16f) -> bloom -> duotone -> film -> afterimage -> screen. same order as the web composer

    bloom: UnrealBloomPass rebuilt. luminosity high pass (threshold 0.65) at half res, 5 mips of separable gaussian (radii 3 5 7 9 11), composite with the 1.0 .8 .6 .4 .2 weights and the radius lerp. strength is driven per frame: 0.18 + pulse stuff, mood scaled, + kick * 0.6

    duotone: the whole frame is luminance mapped onto 4 stops built from A and B only (A*0.05, A, B, B lifted to white 35%). aces fit, 1/1.8 gamma, contrast, split point, dither. the kick flashes B over the frame when a palette lands. verbatim port

    film: three's FilmShader r163, grayscale off, intensity from mood (0.03 calm .. 0.14 wild)

    afterimage: ping pong, damp from mood (0.80 .. 0.94)

    everything is a fullscreen triangle from gl_VertexID, no quad buffers

    shaders live in client/shaders/, loaded at runtime from next to the exe or the source tree. edit, relaunch. hot reload is a v0.6 nicety

7. palette / mood / mutation (done, v0.2)

    palette: exactly two colours, A deep, B bright. makePair ported with its 5 modes (ink+neon, dusk, near-mono, bleached, acid). jumps on a seeded schedule from the runtime stream: calm never hard cuts, wild does 30% of the time, calm jumps half as often. each jump kicks bloom and scale and nudges mutation

    mood: one scalar 0 calm .. 1 wild, pow(u, 1.6) so most seeds land calm/soft. every eye strain effect reads `ml(calm, wild)`. M key cycles CALM SOFT LIVELY WILD, eased over a second. `--mood 0..1` pins it

    mutation clock: dv ~ rate * (0.25 + v), saturates at 1.5. drives uMutate in the berry vert: displacement deepens, a finer second layer grows, drupelets divide finer. calm slows it, wild speeds it

8. rarity (done, v0.4)

    the web had none. this is the new thing and the whole reason for the website. rules:

        tier is rolled on its own sub stream ("rarity"), fixed odds: common 60%, uncommon 25%, rare 10%, epic 4%, legendary 0.9%, mythic 0.1%. deterministic from seed_short, the server recomputes it, the client cannot lie

        tier feeds the generation, not the other way around. I am not scoring "how pretty is this" (impossible, and people would game it). the tier unlocks stuff:

            common: what you get now

            uncommon: +1 extra mutation gen, satellites lean berry (75%)

            rare: a second berry orbiting (its own skin), palette gets a third stop

            epic: compound forced (2 to 4 shapes), 2 extra mutation gens, longer afterimage

            legendary: native mode bleed (see 9), a unique palette family (acid only), rings doubled

            mythic: all of the above + a shape family that only mythic can roll (not written yet, something nobody has seen) + the seed display turns gold lol

        rarity_score (float, in the db) is tier + small deterministic bonuses: lineage length, satellite count, mood extremes. only for sorting the market, never for the tier itself

    why fixed odds and not a lottery on visuals: the server can enforce it from the seed alone, and a mythic is a mythic no matter whose screen it's on

    how it landed: "rarity" sub stream rolled first, the tier feeds everything after it. the unlocks above are all in except the mythic-only family (reserved family 14, still the open question). the second berry is a different generator at 0.35 scale with its own skin on the "twin" stream, orbiting wide. the third stop makes the duotone a five stop ramp (A*0.05, A, C, B, B lifted). the 16 family buckets are in client/src/seed/rarity.cpp and as a comment table in shared/chaos_format.h, the server mirrors that table. the app prints tier, family and score at launch

9. modes (done, v0.3)

    zen, calm, chaos, bleed. 0..3 in the .chaos file. every seed has a native mode (rolled, weights 20 / 35 / 35 / 10). you can override the display mode locally, the native one is what gets valued

        zen: mood pinned 0, no palette jumps ever, mutation clock off, particles only. for people who actually work on their desktop

        calm: mood capped at 0.35, no hard cuts

        chaos: the default. mood as rolled, full range

        bleed: mood pinned wild, hard cuts 60%, afterimage 0.96, plus a smear pass (chromatic split along the kick) that only exists in bleed. this is the one that hurts

    the mode is a post/mood preset, not a different scene. same seed, same shape, same everything, just how much it moves

    how it landed: native mode on its own "mode" sub stream. `--mode zen|calm|chaos|bleed` overrides the display, N cycles, 1-4 set it. the app prints "BLEED native, showing ZEN" so you always know what the seed really is. zen also hides the swarm (satellites, planes, debris, rings) and leaves the berry, the backdrop and the particles. a manual M press still wins over the preset, same as the web

    the smear: chromatic split along a slowly turning direction (never fully closed, bleed always bleeds a bit, 0.0015 at rest) that tears open with the kick (up to 0.0135), plus 7 taps dragged along the same line. sits between the duotone and the film grain. only built when the mode asks for it, zero cost otherwise

10. weekly allowance (v0.8, server side)

    claimable rolls are tickets. the server gives you 1 per week (2026-11-06, was 1 per day banked to 14: ROLL_PERIOD_DAYS / ROLLS_PER_PERIOD / BANK_MAX in config), and only to a signed-in account; the app will not generate anything, previews included, without a session. a preview roll is free and unlimited but can never be claimed (no ticket in the seed)

    allowance lives on the website account, not in the app. the app just asks. offline = preview only

    numbers are tunable, these are v1 floors

11. ownership layer (.chaos file, website registry, value)

    the seed alone is not the asset. the asset is a .chaos file (seed + certificate) that only counts once the website accepts it.

    source of truth: the website. the app renders anything offline, but owning, valuing and transferring needs a google login on the site. blockchain is pushed to v2.0 as an optional mirror, not the registry.

    identity: google account on the website. the per-install key is a subkey, not the identity.

    .chaos file (512 bytes, fixed layout, binary)

        magic "CHAS", version, flags

        seed_full (32 byte blake3), seed_short (first 16, the shareable form), family, tier, mode, mutation_seed

        issued_at (unix ms), instance_id (16 random bytes, generated once per install)

        cert_hmac (hmac-sha256, key k1, over bytes 0..87), payload_hmac (hmac-sha256, key k2, over bytes 0..119)

        nonce (16 bytes, the "current valid copy" marker, rotated on every transfer)

        seed_display (base58 of seed_short) + display_len

        240 bytes reserved padding, then preview_hash (blake3 of the 1920x1080 preview png)

        why fixed binary: trivially parseable, opaque to a text editor, reserved room so version stays at 1 for a while

        preview goes as a hash only, not embedded (keeps the file tiny; the site stores the png)

    keys k1 / k2: derived at runtime from constexpr fragments, not literal strings. this is obfuscation, not cryptography. anyone who disassembles the client gets them. accepted: "until someone figures it out". the website is what gives value, so a forged file alone is worth nothing.

    value model

        rarity = property of the seed. deterministic, computed on both sides, never changes. common / uncommon / rare / epic / legendary / mythic.

        value = property of the market. set by the website at claim time, starts at a per-tier floor (v1: 0.10 / 0.50 / 5 / 25 / 200 / 2000), then moves.

        value = floor(tier) * family_mult * mode_mult * age_bonus * provenance_bonus * supply_discount. multipliers live in the site db, the app never knows them.

    claim flow

        app rolls seed, writes .chaos to the vault folder

        user logs in on site, uploads the file

        site verifies magic / version / both hmacs, rejects if seed_full already claimed or instance_id blacklisted, computes value, inserts seed_full -> owner, returns token_id + value

        app marks the vault entry claimed. from here the local file is a receipt.

    transfer / gift

        owner lists it on the site (price or 0 for gift). other user acquires.

        site swaps owner_id, issues a NEW .chaos with a fresh nonce, revokes the old one.

        old file uploaded again -> rejected (stale nonce). copied file uploaded by anyone else -> rejected (already claimed).

        this is the "even if they share the files they have to confirm on the website" rule. the file is a bearer ticket the site can revoke. only one claim is ever honored, first upload wins by server timestamp. admin can reassign on bugs, no appeals.

    sync: app sends claimed seed_fulls to /api/vault, site returns state per seed, app updates local vault. runs on start, on login, and on a manual button. a seed transferred away on another device shows "transferred out" locally.

    website (decided 2026-11-05, built v0.8)

        cloudflare. one sveltekit app (was the CHAOS/ folder in this repo, since 2026-11-08 its own private repo cuz this one went public), at chaos-eng.tetstack.dev, adapter-cloudflare, pages + workers, D1 (sqlite) for the books, the signing key as a worker secret (never the dev key), google tokens checked with jose against google's jwks (no node-only libs, no Buffer, runs on workers). wrangler.toml in CHAOS/. `npm run deploy`. the api is +server.ts routes under /api, the pages are svelte 5, the registry logic sits in src/lib/server which sveltekit refuses to bundle for the browser. that is the security argument: one framework, one place the private code can live, no second backend to keep honest. (I had started a separate node/hono service, got stopped, fair)

        D1: users, tickets, seeds, files (the current signed bytes, so a buyer gets a real file), transfers (CHAOS/migrations/0001_init.sql, `npm run db:migrate`). no D1 binding = memory store, dev only, nothing persists

        auth: google identity services button on /login, id token to POST /api/auth/google, httpOnly cookie session (jwt, 30 days). the app will use the same jwt as a bearer token (v1.0). ALLOW_FAKE_LOGIN=1 for dev

        endpoints: POST /api/auth/google, GET /api/me, POST /api/ticket {commit}, POST /api/check (public: is this file real, what does the registry know), POST /api/claim, POST /api/list, DELETE /api/revoke/:seed, POST /api/acquire, GET /api/vault, POST /api/sync, GET /api/market, GET /api/seed/:seed, GET /api/pubkey. files travel as base64 in json, 512 bytes is nothing

        pages (v0.9): / (the pitch, how a roll cannot be rigged in four cards, the odds), /check (drop any .chaos: valid or not, tier, value, is this copy current. no sign in. this is what I wanted the web for in the first place), /login (google button, or the dev login when no client id), /vault (allowance, the four-step ticket dance, cards per seed with download / copy / list / unlist), /claim (drop the rolled file, get it back signed), /market (cards, tier filter, acquire), /seed/[hash], an error page. one layout built from the reference page's own stylesheet: --bg #0b0c0b, --silver #ecebe2, hairline --line, flat hairline .key buttons (fill silver on hover), the .chip lcd counters with dseg14, unbounded 800 for the big words, instrument serif italic for the subtitle line, jetbrains mono for everything else, all five fonts served from CHAOS/static/fonts (pulled back out of git history). no gradients behind content, no neon, no purple. gold is legendary/mythic, red is an error, nothing else has colour. GET /api/file/:seed downloads the current signed bytes of a seed you own (the app's sync will use it)

        the registry logic is a port of client/src/chaos_file/format.cpp + client/tools/registry_dev.cpp. client/build/chaos-vectors dumps 400 seeds + a dev-key signed ticket/rolled/claimed set into CHAOS/test/vectors, and vitest proves the ts derives the same tier/family/mode/seed and verifies the same bytes. regenerate the vectors whenever the c++ roll order changes

        value lives in CHAOS/src/lib/server/value.ts, the numbers live in config: floor per tier (0.10 / 0.50 / 5 / 25 / 200 / 2000) * family * mode * age * supply. the client never sees those numbers

        config (v1.3): nothing is inline any more. CHAOS/src/lib/server/config.ts reads every knob from the environment with a default: site name / url / source, session cookie + days, rolls per day, bank max, starting bank, floors, family and mode multipliers, age bonus, supply discount, preview cap, market page size, featured count. locally they come from .dev.vars (gitignored, .dev.vars.example lists all of them), on cloudflare the plain ones sit in wrangler.toml [vars] and the three secrets (signing key, session secret, google client id) go through `wrangler pages secret put`. I move them to cloudflare one by one, the defaults keep working meanwhile. (old, see 13: the dashboard is the only place now) what is NOT config, on purpose: the tier odds, the unlock table, the family buckets, the seed derivation. those are protocol, the c++ and the ts must agree on them, the vectors prove they do

        previews (v1.3): the claim can carry a png. the app shrinks the vault png to 640 wide (box filter, client/src/util/png.cpp shrinkPng) and sends it base64 with the claim; the registry checks it is a png under PREVIEW_MAX_BYTES and keeps it (was r2, D1 table since 11-06, see 13). GET /api/preview/:seed serves it, the market, vault and seed pages show it, featured on the market is the highest tiers listed. search by seed prefix or owner, sort newest / cheapest / priciest / rarest, tier filter, all as url params so a filtered market is a link

        payments: still recorded, not collected. that is v2.0 territory now, it needs a provider account

        acquire hands the buyer a re-signed file with a new nonce. the registry keeps the claimed bytes (files table), so the buyer always gets a real file with the ticket intact, no receipt stubs

        chaos.tetstack.dev stays the old web toy. previews (png) stay on the client until the market wants thumbnails (s3/r2, v1.3)

    repo additions (as it ended up): client/src/chaos_file/ (format, verify, sign), client/src/sync/ (api client, session flows), server/dev/ (where the dev key goes, not committed), shared/chaos_format.h, shared/server_pubkey.h, docs/chaos-file-format.md, docs/ownership-model.md. the registry site is its own repo

    roadmap shift: v0.5 = .chaos format, v0.8 = site backend, v0.9 = site frontend, v1.0 = sync, v1.1 = release. blockchain mint = v2.0 optional.

    cert decision (2026-11-04): server-signed, nothing secret in the client. amended 2026-11-05: commit-reveal, see below

        server holds one ed25519 keypair. only the public key ships in the client binary.

        roll (online): app asks POST /api/ticket while logged in. the weekly allowance is enforced HERE. server returns ticket = ticket_id(16) || user_id(8) || issued_ms(8) || ed25519 sig(64).

        seed_full was blake3(tag || ticket_id || client_random || instance_id). that still had a hole, see "the grind hole" below. now (v3): seed_full = blake3("CHAOS-SEED-v3" || ticket_id || server_random || client_random)

        roll (offline): no ticket, state = preview. renders fine, never claimable. replayable but worthless.

        claim: upload .chaos. server checks ticket sig, ticket unused, ticket user == uploader, recomputes seed_full, derives family/tier/mode itself, computes value, then fills owner_id, claimed_at, nonce and cert_sig = ed25519("CHAOS-CERT-v2" || bytes 8..223). app verifies cert with the embedded pubkey, offline.

        transfer: server rotates nonce, re-signs, old nonce revoked in db. same as before.

        dropped: hmac k1/k2, key obfuscation, client-side cert. forging now needs the server private key. no "until someone figures it out".

        cost: a claimable roll needs the network. preview rolls stay offline.

        the layout lives in shared/chaos_format.h (512 bytes, version 2). docs/chaos-file-format.md explains it.

    how it landed (v0.5)

        client/src/chaos_file/format.cpp: read, write, deriveSeed, verify (layout, seed recompute, ticket sig, cert sig, by state), and the signing half for the server. libsodium ed25519, blake3 for the seed. the registry public key is shared/server_pubkey.h

        the ticket on the wire is 96 bytes: id(16) user(8) issued_ms(8) sig(64). the app takes it with `--ticket t.ticket`, derives the seed from it, and the kept file is state rolled

        verify rules: preview = layout only and no ticket allowed. rolled = layout + ticket sig + seed recompute. claimed = all that + cert sig + owner != 0. offline verify answers "was this ever real", only the registry answers "is this copy current" (nonce)

        chaos-registry-dev: the server's half in c++ until the website exists. keygen, ticket, claim, transfer, verify, one flat text db. it never trusts the client: on claim it recomputes the seed and re-derives tier/family/mode with deriveProps (the same function rollDimension uses, test enforced). the ts server is a port of this file, not a redesign

        dev key: server/dev/server.key, made by `chaos-registry-dev keygen`, not committed (it was, till the repo went public). NOT the prod key. the prod key lives in ~ on my box and as a cloudflare secret, its pubkey is what shared/server_pubkey.h ships

        app side: `--verify f.chaos`, `--import f.chaos` (verify then store, how a claimed or transferred file comes back into the vault), `--vault` now shows valid/INVALID per file

        tested end to end through the binaries: ticket -> roll -> claim -> second claim refused (ticket used) -> transfer -> old copy STALE, new copy CURRENT -> transfer from the stale copy refused -> preview claim refused

    the grind hole (found 2026-11-05, fixed, format v3)

        with the ticket fixed and client_random free, the client could loop client_random a million times a second, derive the tier locally (3 blake3 + a few rng steps), and only submit the mythic one. the server would accept it: the ticket really was used. exactly "reproduce the rare one again and again and sell it"

        fix, the provably fair way games do it: commit-reveal. client draws client_random, sends commit = blake3("CHAOS-COMMIT-v3" || client_random) with the ticket request. the ticket the registry signs carries that commit and its own server_random (drawn after it saw only the commit). seed = blake3(tag || ticket_id || server_random || client_random). the client cannot change its random after seeing server_random (the commit is under the signature), the registry cannot pick server_random for an outcome (it does not know client_random). instance_id left the hash: anything the client can vary freely must stay out of the seed

        verify now checks: ticket sig, commit matches client_random, seed derives, cert sig. the app: `chaos --commit out.reveal` prints the commit, the ticket request carries it, `chaos --ticket t --reveal out.reveal` rolls. the panel's roll tab has both fields. preview rolls are unchanged, they never mattered

        layout v3: ticket grew to 160 bytes on the wire (id, user, issued, commit, server_random, sig), cert now covers bytes 8..288. shared/chaos_format.h has the map. nothing had shipped so no v2 compatibility

    what the previous draft got wrong (kept for the record)

        a. rarity was a local lottery: seed from os.urandom, loop until mythic, claim. fixed by the ticket in the seed hash.

        b. "non-bruteforceable" cert whose keys shipped in the binary. fixed by moving the signature to the server.

    open questions still unanswered: hosting (fly/railway/hetzner), two-step vs direct-to-email transfer (two-step is what shipped).


