    how it landed (v1.0): no oauth inside the app. the site's /login?app=1 signs you in with google and shows the session jwt; the app takes it (`--login-token`, or paste in the account tab, "open the sign-in page" does xdg-open) and keeps it in ~/.config/chaos/session (0600). libsecret later, maybe. the token rides as a bearer header on /api/me, /api/ticket, /api/claim, /api/vault, /api/sync, /api/file/:seed (client/src/sync/api.cpp, libcurl + nlohmann). `--login-dev NAME` for registries with ALLOW_FAKE_LOGIN

        `--roll`: commit, ticket, seed in one go (client/src/sync/session_flow.cpp rollClaimable). the app checks the ticket's signature and that it carries the commit it sent before trusting it. panel: one button when connected

        `--claim f.chaos` / "claim this roll": POST, verify what comes back against our pubkey and the seed, store it over the rolled file, activate it. the by-hand --commit / --ticket / --reveal path still exists for people without a session

        `--sync` / "sync vault": every non-preview seed you hold -> /api/sync -> activation updated (current or transferred away). then /api/vault: anything the registry says is yours that you do not hold (acquired on the web) is fetched from /api/file, verified, stored, activated. tested: a seed sold on the web turned STALE on the seller's app and appeared in the buyer's vault on their next sync

