    how it landed (2026-11-08, testers on telegram, kali / ubuntu / garuda hyprland / fedora): a .deb built on my arch wants arch's glibc so it won't install on debian or ubuntu, obviosly, and the appimage has the same problem cuz appimages don't ship glibc. so packaging/build-portable.sh builds the .deb, .rpm, .tar.gz and the appimage inside a debian bookworm container (podman or docker, glibc 2.36) and those run on kali, ubuntu 22.04+, fedora, wsl. no plasma plugin in those, the plugin has to be built against each distro's own plasma. packaging/build-arch.sh builds the arch package from the tree (tarball + a generated PKGBUILD, makepkg -s installs what's missing), plugin in. bookworm has glfw 3.3 and that one has no glfwGetPlatform / position hints / app id hint, so window.cpp switches on the glfw version (3.3 = x11 only, position after create). and catch2 there is v2 so the tests just get skipped in the container, they run on my box. the files go on the github releases page, nothing built is in git (dist/ and distro/ ignored). a github actions workflow was tried for a day and thrown out, I build locally. imgui was a nested git clone recorded as a submodule pointer with no .gitmodules, so everyone who cloned got an empty folder and the build died on imgui.cpp. vendored the 16 files it actually uses, done. wsl: the app runs under wslg (mesa d3d12 gives gl 4.6), the wallpaper can't, there is no linux desktop to be the wallpaper of

